{
  "name": "unknown_fields_v1",
  "description": "Fixtures that every implementation must REJECT because they carry fields the schema does not define. canonical_json is the canonical encoding of the object including its unknown field, so the rejection is attributable to the unknown field rather than to a non-canonical encoding. Both Swift Codable and Go encoding/json ignore unknown keys by default, so both sides must opt into strict decoding. Silently ignoring an unknown field would let a sender attach meaning the verifier never sees, which is how a widening attack starts.",
